  "raw": {
    "https://www.chalmers.se/en/about-chalmers/work-with-us/assistant-professor-positions/basic-science/": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor in Basic Science",
      "description": "Go to content Login Intranet ( Opens in new tab ) Library ( Opens in new tab ) Svenska sv Search Menu Education Research Collaborate with us About Chalmers Current Departments Assistant professor positions Home About Chalmers Work with us Assistant professor positions Basic Science Available position: Assistant Professor in Basic Science Image 1 of 1 Chalmers now seeks curious and creative individuals for tenure-track Assistant Professors. As an Assistant Professor in Basic Science at Chalmers, you can turn your scientific curiosity into ideas, your ideas into experiments, and your experiments into discoveries. Application closed The application for the seventh global recruitment round for Assistant Professors is now closed. Basic Science: Pushing the boundaries of knowledge Basic Science at Chalmers addresses fundamental questions in mathematics, physics, astronomy, chemistry, material science and the life sciences. Our research spans areas such as mathematical modelling, complex systems, quantum science, fundamental chemistry and physics, biomolecular systems and nanoscale phenomena. Driven by curiosity, we combine theoretical, experimental and computational approaches to advance fundamental understanding and explore new scientific frontiers. Chalmers offers a collaborative and international research environment with strong interdisciplinary connections. The position is a five-year tenure-track appointment with a competitive start-up package including funding for personnel, equipment, and operational costs.You will also get relocation support, mentoring, and leadership training to support your development as an independent research leader and educator. The research spans several departments, including but not limited to: Chemistry and Chemical Engineering Life Sciences Mathematical Sciences Microtechnology and Nanoscience Physics and Astronomy Linked research infrastructures Chalmers e-Commons Chalmers Materials Analysis Laboratory (CMAL) Nanofabrication Laboratory (Myfab) National Academic Infrastructure for Super­computing in Sweden (NAISS) Onsala Space Observatory SciLifeLab Learn more about the offer Brief timeline, available positions and more information about the offer For questions about the process, please contact Recruitment systems support HR department, Chalmers operations support Contact rekr.stodet@chalmers.se For questions about the position, please contact To personal page Margareta Wallquist Advisor , University Executive Office, Chalmers Operations Support Contact margareta.wallquist@chalmers.se +46 31 772 27 18 To personal page To personal page Per Blom HR Partner , CSE Operations Support, Computer Science and Engineering Contact per.blom@chalmers.se +46 31 772 26 53 To personal page Updated 2 June 2026, 13:43 Published 12 December 2023, 17:10 Assistant professor positions Basic Science Batteries Energy Materials Science Mechanical Engineering Nanoscience New Space Production Transport Related content Reputation and ranking World in progress Research infrastructures Research areas Departments For questions about the process, please contact Recruitment systems support HR department, Chalmers operations support Contact rekr.stodet@chalmers.se For questions about the position, please contact To personal page Margareta Wallquist Advisor , University Executive Office, Chalmers Operations Support Contact margareta.wallquist@chalmers.se +46 31 772 27 18 To personal page To personal page Per Blom HR Partner , CSE Operations Support, Computer Science and Engineering Contact per.blom@chalmers.se +46 31 772 26 53 To personal page Contact Chalmers Phone +46-317721000 Mail address Chalmers University of Technology 412 96 Gothenburg E-mail and more contact information Organisation number 556479-5598 Education Education Your studies Our Master's degree programmes Student support Services and tools Canvas learning management system Safe at Chalmers Chalmers student union Shortcuts Shortcuts Work at C