    "https://www.chalmers.se/en/about-chalmers/work-with-us/assistant-professor-positions/batteries/": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor in Batteries",
      "description": "Available position: Assistant Professor in Batteries | Chalmers Go to content Login Intranet ( Opens in new tab ) Library ( Opens in new tab ) Svenska sv Search Menu Education Research Collaborate with us About Chalmers Current Departments Assistant professor positions Home About Chalmers Work with us Assistant professor positions Batteries Available position: Assistant Professor in Batteries Image 1 of 1 Chalmers now seeks curious and creative individuals for tenure-track Assistant Professors. As an Assistant Professor in Batteries at Chalmers, you can turn your scientific curiosity into ideas, your ideas into experiments, and your experiments into discoveries. Application closed The application for the seventh global recruitment round for Assistant Professors is now closed. Advancing batteries for a sustainable future Battery technologies are central to the transition towards electrified transport and sustainable energy systems. At Chalmers, we conduct research across the battery value chain, from materials and electrochemistry to modelling, diagnostics and control of battery systems. Through national initiatives such as COMPEL and close collaboration with industry, we develop knowledge and technologies that enable safer, more efficient and longer-lasting energy storage solutions for the future. The position is a five-year tenure-track appointment with a competitive start-up package including funding for personnel, equipment, and operational costs.You will also get relocation support, mentoring, and leadership training to support your development as an independent research leader and educator. Particular emphasis for this position is placed on modelling, estimation and control of battery systems, including not only current lithium-ion chemistries but also next-generation technologies, as well as the integration of batteries in electrified energy and transport systems. The position will be primarily based at the department of Electrical Engineering , but the research will span several departments including but not limited to: Chemistry and Chemical Engineering Mechanical Engineering Microtechnology and Nanoscience Physics and Astronomy Linked research infrastructure Compel battery initiative Learn more about the offer Brief timeline, available positions and more information about the offer For questions about the process, please contact Recruitment systems support HR department, Chalmers operations support Contact rekr.stodet@chalmers.se For questions about the position, please contact To personal page Aleksandar Matic Head of Division , Physics and Astronomy Contact matic@chalmers.se +46 31 772 51 76 To personal page Updated 2 June 2026, 13:43 Published 12 December 2023, 17:10 Leave feedback Assistant professor positions Basic Science Batteries Energy Materials Science Mechanical Engineering Nanoscience New Space Production Transport Related content Reputation and ranking World in progress Research infrastructures Research areas Departments For questions about the process, please contact Recruitment systems support HR department, Chalmers operations support Contact rekr.stodet@chalmers.se For questions about the position, please contact To personal page Aleksandar Matic Head of Division , Physics and Astronomy Contact matic@chalmers.se +46 31 772 51 76 To personal page Contact Chalmers Phone +46-317721000 Mail address Chalmers University of Technology 412 96 Gothenburg E-mail and more contact information Organisation number 556479-5598 Education Education Your studies Our Master's degree programmes Student support Services and tools Canvas learning management system Safe at Chalmers Chalmers student union Shortcuts Shortcuts Work at Chalmers Press and media Whistleblowing at Chalmers Safety and emergency situations Supplier information Chalmers University of Technology Foundation About the website About the website Cookies Processing of personal data Accessibility statement Service Disruptions at Chalme