    "https://www.chalmers.se/en/about-chalmers/work-with-us/assistant-professor-positions/materials-science/": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor in Materials Science",
      "description": "Available position: Assistant Professor in Materials Science | Chalmers Go to content Login Intranet ( Opens in new tab ) Library ( Opens in new tab ) Svenska sv Search Menu Education Research Collaborate with us About Chalmers Current Departments Assistant professor positions Home About Chalmers Work with us Assistant professor positions Materials Science Available position: Assistant Professor in Materials Science Image 1 of 1 Chalmers now seeks curious and creative individuals for tenure-track Assistant Professors. As an Assistant Professor in Materials Science at Chalmers, you can turn your scientific curiosity into ideas, your ideas into experiments, and your experiments into discoveries. Application closed The application for the seventh global recruitment round for Assistant Professors is now closed. Advancing materials science for a sustainable future Materials science at Chalmers combines fundamental research with applications that address major societal challenges. Our research spans the entire materials value chain, from theory and modelling to synthesis, characterisation and evaluation of material properties. We focus on materials for energy applications, materials for health applications, and materials for green transitions. Through interdisciplinary collaboration and strong links to industry, we develop advanced materials that enable sustainable technologies and future innovations. The position is a five-year tenure-track appointment with a competitive start-up package including funding for personnel, equipment, and operational costs.You will also get relocation support, mentoring, and leadership training to support your development as an independent research leader and educator. The research spans several departments, including but not limited to: Architecture and Civil Engineering Chemistry and Chemical Engineering Life Sciences Mechanical Engineering Microtechnology and Nanoscience Physics and Astronomy Linked research infrastructures and centres ARTEMI Chalmers Materials Analysis Laboratory (CMAL) MAX IV Nanofabrication Laboratory (Myfab) National Academic Infrastructure for Super­computing in Sweden (NAISS) The Swedish NMR Centre Wallenberg Initiative Materials Science for Sustainability (WISE) Wallenberg Wood Science Center (WWSC) Learn more about the offer Brief timeline, available positions and more information about the offer For questions about the process, please contact Recruitment systems support HR department, Chalmers operations support Contact rekr.stodet@chalmers.se For questions about the position, please contact To personal page Leif Asp Full Professor , Computational Mechanics and Materials Engineering, Mechanical Engineering Contact leif.asp@chalmers.se +46 31 772 15 43 To personal page Updated 2 June 2026, 13:43 Published 12 December 2023, 17:10 Assistant professor positions Basic Science Batteries Energy Materials Science Mechanical Engineering Nanoscience New Space Production Transport Related content Reputation and ranking World in progress Research infrastructures Research areas Departments For questions about the process, please contact Recruitment systems support HR department, Chalmers operations support Contact rekr.stodet@chalmers.se For questions about the position, please contact To personal page Leif Asp Full Professor , Computational Mechanics and Materials Engineering, Mechanical Engineering Contact leif.asp@chalmers.se +46 31 772 15 43 To personal page Contact Chalmers Phone +46-317721000 Mail address Chalmers University of Technology 412 96 Gothenburg E-mail and more contact information Organisation number 556479-5598 Education Education Your studies Our Master's degree programmes Student support Services and tools Canvas learning management system Safe at Chalmers Chalmers student union Shortcuts Shortcuts Work at Chalmers Press and media Whistleblowing at Chalmers Safety and emergency situations Supplier information Chalmers University of Technology Fo