    "https://www.chalmers.se/en/about-chalmers/work-with-us/assistant-professor-positions/transport/": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor in Transport",
      "description": "Available position: Assistant Professor in Transport | Chalmers Go to content Login Intranet ( Opens in new tab ) Library ( Opens in new tab ) Svenska sv Search Menu Education Research Collaborate with us About Chalmers Current Departments Assistant professor positions Home About Chalmers Work with us Assistant professor positions Transport Available position: Assistant Professor in Transport Image 1 of 1 Chalmers now seeks curious and creative individuals for tenure-track Assistant Professors. As an Assistant Professor in Transport at Chalmers, you can turn your scientific curiosity into ideas, your ideas into experiments, and your experiments into discoveries. Application closed The application for the seventh global recruitment round for Assistant Professors is now closed. Advancing climate-neutral and safe transport systems Transport research at Chalmers contributes to the development of sustainable, safe and efficient mobility systems for people and goods. In close collaboration with industry, public authorities and international partners, we address key challenges related to freight and passenger transport, logistics and electromobility, transport technologies, and automated and connected transport safety. Located in Gothenburg, a major hub for the automotive and transport industries, Chalmers offers unique opportunities to develop and test new transport solutions that support the transition to climate-neutral mobility. The position as Assistant Professor comes with a five-year tenure track position with a generous start-up package, relocation support and mentoring, and leadership training to further your development as research leader and teacher. The research spans several departments, including but not limited to: Architecture and Civil Engineering Chemistry and Chemical Engineering Computer Science and Engineering Electrical Engineering Environmental and Energy Sciences Mathematical Sciences Mechanical Engineering Microtechnology and Nanoscience Physics and Astronomy Technology Management and Economics Linked research centres: Northern LEAD SAFER – Vehicle and Transport Safety Centre TechForH2 Learn more about the offer Brief timeline, available positions and more information about the offer For questions about the process, please contact Recruitment systems support HR department, Chalmers operations support Contact rekr.stodet@chalmers.se For questions about the position, please contact To personal page Balázs Adam Kulcsár Full Professor , Systems and Control, Electrical Engineering Contact kulcsar@chalmers.se +46 31 772 17 85 To personal page To personal page Ala Arvidsson Associate Professor , Supply and Operations Management, Technology Management and Economics Contact ala.arvidsson@chalmers.se +46 31 772 13 72 To personal page Updated 2 June 2026, 13:45 Published 12 December 2023, 17:10 Assistant professor positions Basic Science Batteries Energy Materials Science Mechanical Engineering Nanoscience New Space Production Transport Related content Reputation and ranking World in progress Research infrastructures Research areas Departments For questions about the process, please contact Recruitment systems support HR department, Chalmers operations support Contact rekr.stodet@chalmers.se For questions about the position, please contact To personal page Balázs Adam Kulcsár Full Professor , Systems and Control, Electrical Engineering Contact kulcsar@chalmers.se +46 31 772 17 85 To personal page To personal page Ala Arvidsson Associate Professor , Supply and Operations Management, Technology Management and Economics Contact ala.arvidsson@chalmers.se +46 31 772 13 72 To personal page Contact Chalmers Phone +46-317721000 Mail address Chalmers University of Technology 412 96 Gothenburg E-mail and more contact information Organisation number 556479-5598 Education Education Your studies Our Master's degree programmes Student support Services and tools Canvas learning management system Safe at Chalmers 